// REQUIRES: host-linux-amd64, gdb
// RUN: %gopp build %S/Inputs/scopes.gopp -o %t
// RUN: timeout 60 gdb -batch -nx -x %S/Inputs/scopes.gdb %t 2>&1 | FileCheck %s
// P04.12, D4.7: shadowed names, nested blocks and loops. In each block the
// debugger shows the variable of that block (the innermost first), not the
// one it shadows; a variable whose block has ended is not shown; and a global
// is not hidden by a local of the same name (it is `main.x`).

// CHECK: @@INNER
// The block `{ x := y*2; y := x+5 }`: the inner x and y, then the function's y.
// CHECK: x = 16
// CHECK-NEXT: y = 21
// CHECK-NEXT: y = 8
// CHECK: $1 = 16
// CHECK-NEXT: $2 = 21
// CHECK: @@LOOP1
// The loop body: its x and the loop's i, then the function's y.
// CHECK: x = 100
// CHECK-NEXT: i = 0
// CHECK-NEXT: y = 8
// CHECK: $3 = 100
// CHECK-NEXT: $4 = 0
// CHECK: @@LOOP2
// CHECK: x = 101
// CHECK-NEXT: i = 1
// CHECK-NEXT: y = 108
// After the loop and the block only the function's y is a local; x is the
// parameter.
// CHECK: @@AFTER
// CHECK: y = 209
// CHECK-NEXT: $5 = 209
// CHECK: x = 7
// main's x shadows the global.
// CHECK: @@MAIN
// CHECK: x = 7
// CHECK: $6 = 1000
